<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup Label="General">
    <Version>$(BUILD_BUILDNUMBER)</Version>
    <Copyright>© Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.</Copyright>
    <TargetFrameworks>net6.0;netcoreapp2.1;net472;netstandard2.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <CheckEolTargetFramework>false</CheckEolTargetFramework>
    <KustoDir>$([System.IO.Path]::GetFullPath("$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\..\.."))</KustoDir>
    <OutputPath>$(KustoDir)\bin\$(Configuration)\Projects\$(MSBuildProjectName)</OutputPath>
    <IntermediateOutputPath>$(KustoDir)\obj\$(Configuration)\$(MSBuildProjectName)</IntermediateOutputPath>
    <BaseIntermediateOutputPath>$(IntermediateOutputPath)</BaseIntermediateOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\Kusto.Packages\EULA-agreement.txt">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\Kusto.Packages\MSFT.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Label="NuGet">
    <Authors>Microsoft</Authors>
    <Owners>microsoft,microsoft_kusto</Owners>
    <PackageTags>kusto</PackageTags>
    <PackageId>Microsoft.Azure.Kusto.Language</PackageId>
    <Product>Azure Data Explorer (Kusto) language service</Product>
    <Description>Language service (parser, syntax model, and intellisense API) for Azure Data Explorer (Kusto)</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
13.0.0
The language service has always assumed en-US conventions for query text, as programming languages
generally do, but it read those conventions from the host's ambient culture. It now applies them
directly, so behavior no longer varies with the machine's ambient culture across .NET Framework,
.NET, and the JavaScript (Bridge) build. Review the following if your application ran under a
non-invariant culture.

- Literal parsing is invariant, and now agrees with the engine. Numeric and date/time literals
  (real, decimal, long, int, datetime, timespan) are parsed with the invariant culture instead of
  CultureInfo.CurrentCulture. Under cultures that use a comma as the decimal separator, real(1,5)
  is no longer 1.5: like the engine, the comma is read as a group separator, so the value is 15.
  Datetime literals are read in the invariant format rather than the host's date order. A group
  separator is only accepted in the integral part of a real literal, so real(1.5,3) and real(1e3,5)
  are invalid on every target.
- Case-insensitive matching is ordinal. Name, wildcard, and host name matching no longer use
  culture-sensitive casing. Most visibly, under Turkish-like cultures 'I' and 'i' now match each
  other, and characters such as U+0131 and U+017F no longer match their ASCII look-alikes.
- Wildcard patterns match case-insensitively in every segment. Previously a middle segment, such as
  SAMPLE in *SAMPLE*, was matched case-sensitively even when matching ignored case; it now matches
  Samples the same way a leading or trailing segment does.
- Completion items are ordered ordinally. Items with the same rank and priority were previously
  sorted by the host's culture, so orderings differed under cultures such as cs-CZ and da-DK.
  Punctuation now sorts by character code; culture sorting previously all but ignored hyphens.
- Supplementary-plane characters fold consistently. Case-insensitive matching of characters outside
  the Basic Multilingual Plane now agrees across targets, including on hosts whose
  OrdinalIgnoreCase folds per UTF-16 code unit and therefore did not previously fold them.

Unchanged: a literal that cannot be parsed still yields the type's default value rather than a
diagnostic. Literal values are computed on demand rather than during parsing and analysis, so there
is no general point at which such a failure could be reported.

Known limitation: a small set of Basic Multilingual Plane characters (for example U+00B5 MICRO SIGN
and U+03C2 GREEK SMALL LETTER FINAL SIGMA) still fold differently between hosts that use NLS casing
and hosts that use ICU casing.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>true</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <PackageLicenseFile>EULA-agreement.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://aka.ms/kdocs</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageIcon>MSFT.png</PackageIcon>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild Condition="'$(KUSTO_PACKAGES_DISABLE_PACKAGING)' != '1'">true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <PackageOutputPath>$(KustoDir)\bin\$(Configuration)\Packages</PackageOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>